{
  "_readme": "GAME CONTENT, DRAFT PENDING PRODUCER REVIEW (region and seal names, level bands, map rules). The region campaign: ten regions cover levels 1-100 in order, each played as Stages expeditions (node maps generated by the runtime NodeMapGenerator from MapRules and a seed, Slay-the-Spire style: Paths walks over Lanes x (Layers - 1) rows, row 0 Battle, RestLayer all Rest (Camp: train one beast), the top a single Gate (stages before the last) or the region's Boss (the last stage); other nodes drawn by NodeWeights, Elite/Rest/Shop never following their own type, no Elite below EliteMinLayer, MinElites-MaxElites Elites and at most MaxShops Shops per map). Node level: MinLevel + floor(t x (MaxLevel - MinLevel) / T), t = stage x (Layers - 1) + row, T = Stages x (Layers - 1); Elites +EliteLevelOffset, Gates +GateLevelOffset, the Boss exactly MaxLevel. Battle nodes draw a shape by the region's ShapeWeights (encounter-library.json shapes); Elites and generated Gates use EliteShapeId; the Boss fields BossTemplateId (encounter-library.json Templates) and grants BossRewardSealId. Seals are key items: the beast level cap is the highest owned seal's LevelCap, or StartingLevelCap (first region max + LevelCapMargin). A region's own MapRules override the library's when its Layers is above 0. Validated by RegionLibraryValidator (the Editor importer Beast Craft/Data/Import Regions, the EditMode tests, Tooling/BalanceSim --mode campaign); paced by --mode campaign (docs/balance/campaign-pacing-report.md). See docs/design/progression-and-saves.md, 'Region campaign'.",
